Package: ggsaveR
Title: A Wrapper for 'ggplot2::ggsave' with Extra Features
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Anders Hagen", "Jarmund", , "anders.h.jarmund@ntnu.no", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A drop-in replacement for 'ggsave()' from 'ggplot2', configured
    through global options so that existing scripts need no changes. Saves
    plots to several formats and sizes at once with consistent file names,
    protects existing files from being overwritten, writes greyscale and
    colour vision deficiency versions for checking colour palettes, embeds
    the code, data and session information in PNG files for
    reproducibility, and keeps a log of every saved figure.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Depends: 
    R (>= 4.1.0),
    ggplot2
Encoding: UTF-8
